  "note": "Annual election of one-third of the Ballyclare Urban Council, January 1929. Four nominations were received for three vacancies, one was invalid, and the three valid candidates were returned unopposed (Belfast Telegraph, 7 January 1929, p. 4). Four nominations were lodged; the paper of Mr. Francis Blair, cinema manager, was invalid, so there was no contest. Returned unopposed."
